{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545904-mtaw-2e-one-shot-play-rules","id":1545904,"title":"[MtAw 2E] One-shot play rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-14T19:02:15-08:00","id":1545904,"title":"[MtAw 2E] One-shot play rules","content":"So I now run what is a chronicle made of series of One-shot adventures, 'one story for one century of Orders history'. Generally, I think that I have good grasp of story parts and can work with <b>Mage</b> mechanics after circa 15 years with this gameline. \ud83d\ude09 ( Having 4 years pause for other RPGs. )<br /> <br /> The Advancement is also solved by simple thing - for each new Story we made new PCs, so literally for each few weeks players can try different things with new character. And players can make '<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/rpg/comments/letg63/can_anyone_recommend_a_ttrpg_with_a_legacy/\" target=\"_blank\">legacy RPG</a> characters' -<i> 'my new PC is grandson of one from previous adventure'</i> or <i>'my new PC have Soul Stone of Master XYZ'</i>. This kind of things.<br /> <br /> However, there is one particular mechanical-setting thing in 2E gameline that do not work with that model - <b>Obsessions</b>. ( Of course it's Obsessions \ud83d\ude44 )<br /> <br /> MtAw 2E corebook <i><b>'Obsessions as special magical Aspirations</b></i><b>'</b> works when player have TIME with character. Like several sessions for that. Player understand what things his character want to dwell as side projects, as Modus Operandi on her magic, deeper the magical style. However in '<i>One-shot series chronicles</i>' it will not work - as players before <i>'get to know'</i> character - they change it for another, on next one-shot. And here comes my alternatives for that...<br /> <br /> <b>Obsessions for One-Shots</b><br /> In One-Shots games, Obsessions are not giving Experience - instead, they point 'magical specialties' in general magic and Occult of character.<br /> <br /> <b>System: </b>Instead for giving extra Arcane Beats, <i><b>Obsessions now give constant +3 bonus on things related to it, just like Skill Speciality would</b>.</i> Instead to Skill Speciality, this bonus is also to Instant Casting, Attributes rolls - or any roll made by Obsession having character in this particular field. Her Supernal Obsession literally overflows her to make things with it real.<br /> <br /> <b>Reasoning:</b> I decide on +3 bonus not without consideration. Normal Skill Speciality of +1 is generally negligible in later <b>Mage</b> game, with Arcana 3+ and Gnosis 3+, when character can literally generate new Skills and Attributes dots for themselves. Also, setting-wise, Obsessions are... well, Obsessions. Character are literally thinking on them any time they do not think on their Aspirations or day-to-day life. And thirdly, from <b>Storypath</b> I wanted to incorporate hard '<i>and you get extra bonus success'</i> from Enhancement. It seems fitting to add here. And calculations point that <b>CoD</b> rules +3 dice bonus should generate 1 success, normally. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> <b>So, what do you think about that rules Hack for One-Shot games?</b><br /> <br /> BTW - <b>Aspirations system I simply change to what CoD 2E books says for NPC </b>- When character recover Aspiration in One-Shot, she get's back Willpower point. I think about making it possible for character to get Mana instead of Willpower if they like - it's also much smaller economy on their part in One-Shots, so generating Mana is not as such hurdle. Also, it sort already works like that with Vows from <b>Signs of Sorcery</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-15-2024, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}